{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties","id":1355114,"title":"Skill Specialties","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-15T20:54:25-08:00","id":1355114,"title":"Skill Specialties","content":"A few questions regarding Skill Specialties<br /> <br /> * With a skill specialty in a Skill at 3 dots, does the 1 point enhancement apply to the original skill?<br /> * From the quoted text below I do not gather that it does.<br /> * Are the following examples correct? <div align=\"center\"><b><u>EXAMPLE #1</u></b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>Shot Thug with Pistol</i></b><br /> 6d +1e vs Defense<br /> 3 Aim (Specialty: Pistols)<br /> 3 Dexterity<br /> 1e Weapon Enhancement<br /> <br /> <b><i>Intimidate thug to beat feet</i></b><br /> 6d +2e vs Resolve or Composure<br /> 3 Command<br /> 3 Presence<br /> 1e Waiving a pistol as show of force<br /> 1e Specialty<br /> (100% higher enhancement than primary skill) <div align=\"center\"><b><u>EXAMPLE #2</u></b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i>Shot Thug with Pistol</i></b><br /> 8d +1e vs Defense<br /> 5 Aim (Specialty: Pistols)<br /> 3 Dexterity<br /> 1e Weapon Enhancement<br /> <br /> <i><b>Intimidate thug to beat feet</b></i><br /> 8d +4e vs Resolve of Composure<br /> 5 Command<br /> 3 Presence<br /> 1e Waiving a pistol as show of force<br /> 3e Specialty<br /> (300% higher enhancement than primary skill)<br /> <br /> If they are correct does it seem odd that using the Skill Specialty granted because of your <i><b>expertise</b></i> in that skill grants a a bonus far greater on another skill than the skill it is learned from, if all other points are equal. What am I missing? The example in the quote compares the characters specialty against another character that does not have said specialty, which makes perfect sense. However it does not appear to compare itself to the characters own level of skill (primary skill vs other skill), as it provides a greater enhancement to the <u>other</u> skill.<br /> <br /> My final question regarding this, is what is everyone else doing? Are you running Skill Specialties RAW (Rules as Written) or are you house ruling this in some way.<br /> <br /> Thank you<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> SPECIALTIES<br /> A Specialty is narrowly focused <b><i>expertise</i></b> within a Skill. For example, Aim grants skill with all ranged weapons, but a character may have a Specialty in Pistols. Once a character has a Specialty, she may apply that expertise as a 1-point Enhancement to other Skills. Each dot the character has in the Skill at or above three dots adds an extra point of Enhancement. For example, a character might apply her Pistols Specialty from Aim to an action using her Culture Skill to suggest a deeper knowledge and understanding of gun shows than another character who is equally adept in Culture might have. If the character had four dots in the Aim Skill, the Enhancement would be worth two points. A character gains the ability to purchase Specialties when her Skill rating is three or higher.<br /> <br /> - TC Core 45 </div> </div> </div>Posted in OnyxPath Forums &amp; Discord","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 12-16-2019, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T21:10:24-08:00","id":1355118,"title":"","content":"I've only been giving +1e regardless of the dots, so I've been doing it wrong. But I think I'll keep doing it wrong because the equivalent of like +9 dice to a skill because a character is really good at another skill is just way too much benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T21:49:58-08:00","id":1355124,"title":"","content":"It seemed absurd to me that somebody with a Skill Speciality Pistols could do everything better with Pistols except shooting them at something. When you gain a Specialty you get 1 E regardless of dots in the skill. Aim with a Specialty in Pistols gives you 1E when shooting pistols. If you can make a decent case for it, you may use that specialty in conjunction with another skill. If you have a specialty in Rifles and want to make a Cultures check to see what you know about <a href=\"https://www.americanhunter.org/articles/2013/10/16/do-the-ten-black-kings-exist/\" target=\"_blank\">Ten Black Kings</a> that would work. Like Skill Tricks, you get one free at char creations assuming at least three dots. You may (but don't have to) buy others with XP when you raise a skill to 3 dots and again and 4 and 5 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T23:08:54-08:00","id":1355131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties#post1355114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few questions regarding Skill Specialties<br /> <br /> * With a skill specialty in a Skill at 3 dots, does the 1 point enhancement apply to the original skill?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the Enhancement applies to other skills only.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T09:36:10-08:00","id":1355200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355131#post1355131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, the Enhancement applies to other skills only.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for your responses.<br /> <br /> My stumbling block is that the skill specialty makes you better at the other skill than the skill you learned the specialty from. So the mechanic says if I am equal at aiming/shooting to intimidating (to use my example above), and I have expertise at pistols this makes me better at intimidating with a pistol than aiming and shotting a pistol.<br /> <br /> When creating characters with the players this was the initial response from 2 out of 4 players. They were like, say what? So one player within seconds of understanding the rule, said so if I take Humanities 5 dots and a speciaties in geometry/precision angles, then I can apply a +3 to my firearms or maybe a pool-8 ball shots, darts, on a case by case basis. He is not shy about asking, either. His mind set is don't put a rule in front of me, and not expect that I will use it.<br /> <br /> Now keep in mind I am not debating if I would or would not allow the specialty in this or that situation. I really enjoy the Storypath mechanics as it does a great job at focusing on roleplaying instead of ruleplaying or rollplaying. And I may feel the need to houserule this, but I am trying to get feedback that for those of you that have said yes that is correct and yes we agree with this, what do you think of the other skill now becoming the primary skill and the specialty bumping combat up to +3e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T09:37:32-08:00","id":1355201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355131#post1355131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, the Enhancement applies to other skills only.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, assuming that Int and Dex are equal and that Cultures/Aim are at 3 but that I have a Specialty with Pistols, that means that this character is better at knowing the history/etc of Pistols than actually shooting them?<br /> <br /> Does this mean that if I have Culture (Weaponry) that I can get Enhancements to Aim and Close Combat?<br /> <br /> Because that seems a little silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T10:01:26-08:00","id":1355204,"title":"","content":"I thought this was a particularly fresh take on Specialties in the realm of storyX games. Especially with the set mission statement of constrained dice pools.<br /> <br /> The other contextual thing is that Skill dots are at a real premium in the current chargen for the various Trinity games, so your good skill gets to help buoy your other skills.<br /> <br /> If you want to be better at shooting, buy another dot, or get a new skill trick. It is new and different, and I'm not espousing it as a superior take on specialties, but I think it is a valid one. Also, exceedingly easy to houserule, as it doesn't have too many knock on effects on the rest of the system.<br /> <br /> Also, Traditional Storyteller style Specialties are handled better by Edges in TC in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T10:49:57-08:00","id":1355211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355201#post1355201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, assuming that Int and Dex are equal and that Cultures/Aim are at 3 but that I have a Specialty with Pistols, that means that this character is better at knowing the history/etc of Pistols than actually shooting them?<br /> <br /> Does this mean that if I have Culture (Weaponry) that I can get Enhancements to Aim and Close Combat?<br /> <br /> Because that seems a little silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think of it this way:<br /> <br /> Imagine two people with equal Int and Dex and equal Culture and Aim (3 or higher,) but one has an Aim specialty in Pistols and one has an Aim specialty in Automatic Rifles. Which one is more likely to know something about that US Civil War pistol you have?<br /> <br /> Also, it makes narrative sense for a character who has studied the tenets of Bushido and the history of samurai to be better with a katana than with a broadsword. (If nothing else, he's more likely to own and practice with a katana than a broadsword.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T11:43:55-08:00","id":1355221,"title":"","content":"I really like the way specialities work to help other skills. I just think anything above +1e is excessive. Maybe I'd even go with using the original rules but changing +1e to +3e to +1 die to +3 dice. That's sorta going against the standard &quot;don't add dice&quot; thing in the system, but it's less extreme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T11:56:54-08:00","id":1355226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355211#post1355211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Think of it this way:<br /> <br /> Imagine two people with equal Int and Dex and equal Culture and Aim (3 or higher,) but one has an Aim specialty in Pistols and one has an Aim specialty in Automatic Rifles. Which one is more likely to know something about that US Civil War pistol you have?<br /> <br /> Also, it makes narrative sense for a character who has studied the tenets of Bushido and the history of samurai to be better with a katana than with a broadsword. (If nothing else, he's more likely to own and practice with a katana than a broadsword.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with everything you said. None of those are my challenge. My challenge in your example is the single person has equal Aim/Culture and Int/Dex and an aim specialty in Pistoles he is better at knowledge than shooting which is how he gained the knowledge. I am only comparing his Culture+Int+Specialty vs his Aim+Dex. I am not comparing him against anyone else.<br /> <br /> In your second example which is even better. His study in the tenets of bushido makes him a better swords master than a learned man of the tenets.<br /> <br /> Do you get what I am saying? Comparing primary skill to the other skill of equal value a +1e makes their bonus 100% better than the skill it was derived from.<br /> <br /> As mentioned above very easy to house rule. I make it a point to pound a rule with a hammer before I change it. Most response automatically compare to the other party or another target which is not the challenge I see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T12:09:08-08:00","id":1355231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355204#post1355204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought this was a particularly fresh take on Specialties in the realm of storyX games. Especially with the set mission statement of constrained dice pools.<br /> <br /> The other contextual thing is that Skill dots are at a real premium in the current chargen for the various Trinity games, so your good skill gets to help buoy your other skills.<br /> <br /> If you want to be better at shooting, buy another dot, or get a new skill trick. It is new and different, and I'm not espousing it as a superior take on specialties, but I think it is a valid one. Also, exceedingly easy to houserule, as it doesn't have too many knock on effects on the rest of the system.<br /> <br /> Also, Traditional Storyteller style Specialties are handled better by Edges in TC in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree I love the constrained dice pools or bounded accuracy of Dice pools or Enhancement bonuses. Having seen vampire games and exalted games throw handfuls of dice around I am a huge fan of the story path method.<br /> <br /> My only challenge with skill specialties is they make the other skill better than the original skill. So players will tend to take the other skill as a specialty to benefit the skill they want. And as you point out very easy to house rule a plus 1 to the skill and a plus 1 to the other skill and be done with it.<br /> <br /> And I agree skill tricks are amazing and specialties are not meant to come anywhere near the ability those skill trick gives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T12:55:11-08:00","id":1355242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355226#post1355226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am only comparing his Culture+Int+Specialty vs his Aim+Dex. I am not comparing him against anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which I feel is a mistake. It's hard to compare one skill to another, especially combat to non-combat since difficulties are determined differently. 3 successes on a Culture roll mean something different than 3 successes on an Aim roll. The Culture roll is going to give you a good amount of success while that Aim roll could very well miss with a good defense roll. That's why I was comparing two people but the same skills. It compares like to like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8719,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","user":"Florin","date":".  Edited to fix grammer, spelling, and clarity. 12-16-2019, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T12:58:08-08:00","id":1355243,"title":"","content":"Specialties don\u2019t make the other skill better than the original skill - you have the same dice pool and the same chance failure. What they do is give you a little edge over your equally skilled colleagues in situations where the breadth of knowledge and experience in your narrow specialty applies. You\u2019re not better at Culture than you are at Aiming. Six dice for both in your example. Succeed or fail with the same percentages. But once you\u2019ve made that Culture check, if the topic involves pistols, the fact that you\u2019re so experienced with pistols through Aim might help you against the guy who is as culturally skilled (or more) as you, but doesn\u2019t know about pistols specifically.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also a two way street here. Take a specialty in culture and use it when it applies to combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T15:05:19-08:00","id":1355277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355242#post1355242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which I feel is a mistake. It's hard to compare one skill to another, especially combat to non-combat since difficulties are determined differently. 3 successes on a Culture roll mean something different than 3 successes on an Aim roll. The Culture roll is going to give you a good amount of success while that Aim roll could very well miss with a good defense roll. That's why I was comparing two people but the same skills. It compares like to like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree and disagree. In my original example <br /> <br /> Aim and Shoot vs Defense<br /> Command and Intimidate vs Resolve or Composure<br /> <br /> May be the same as defense if Resolve or Composure are higher than Stamina or using a static antagonist pool.<br /> <br /> Rolled or static should shake out about the same with the Specialty providing a &quot;better&quot; end result on a successful roll.<br /> <br /> I agree it will not shake out on some skills. Two non-combat skills compared would. <br /> <br /> A quote I heard on a tv show plays in my mind ...<br /> <br /> &quot; when you are a hammer every problem in the world looks like a nail &quot;<br /> <br /> Best regards and thank you for all the feedback","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T16:28:01-08:00","id":1355291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355243#post1355243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specialties don\u2019t make the other skill better than the original skill - you have the same dice pool and the same chance failure. What they do is give you a little edge over your equally skilled colleagues in situations where the breadth of knowledge and experience in your narrow specialty applies. You\u2019re not better at Culture than you are at Aiming. Six dice for both in your example. Succeed or fail with the same percentages. But once you\u2019ve made that Culture check, if the topic involves pistols, the fact that you\u2019re so experienced with pistols through Aim might help you against the guy who is as culturally skilled (or more) as you, but doesn\u2019t know about pistols specifically.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also a two way street here. Take a specialty in culture and use it when it applies to combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that. That's the part that makes this kind of silly.<br /> <br /> Assuming equivalent Attributes, let's take two folks. Both have Aim and Technology at 3 Dots. Person 1 has an Aim Specialty with Pistols. Person 2 has a Technology Specialty with Weapons.<br /> <br /> At this point Person 1 is better with building, fixing and designing Pistols than Person 2. Person 2 will be able to shoot pistols better than Person 1.<br /> <br /> And as far as &quot;better&quot; with dice pools, etc, the fact of the matter is that all else being equal, a person with an Enhancement toward something is generally going to be more successful at that something than someone without an Enhancement. They're called Enhancements for a reason.<br /> <br /> I get part of it. You want people to use their Specialties in different/interesting/wider ways. But they still can.<br /> <br /> A Person with Aim (Pistols) gets a 1E when shooting Pistols. And with the GM's okay, they can apply that 1E when holding forth with Cultures on the history of Pistols. Or when trying to repair a broken Pistol with Technology. Meanwhile, the person with Technology (Weaponry) should be &quot;better&quot; at fixing, building, upgrading weapons. And might also be able to intelligently discuss the history of certain kinds of weapons.<br /> <br /> Finally, I think a 1E with a Specialty is sufficient given how widely it could potentially be applied.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T18:00:00-08:00","id":1355302,"title":"","content":"I honestly prefer this way than a free enhancement on the same skill in the right sircunstance for some reason only, cross specialising.<br /> <br /> Imagine you want to create the Perfect Shooter, give him 5 dots and specialist in the weapon of choice, it\u2019s boring. Now imagine you are a specialist in technology for anti-vehicle shots, or have a good training in medicine to pick the perfect spot to shoot, or a specialist in personal armor to go thru armored enemies. It gives a depth to the character even if you want to min max your char...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T18:59:43-08:00","id":1355316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355302#post1355302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly prefer this way than a free enhancement on the same skill in the right sircunstance for some reason only, cross specialising.<br /> <br /> Imagine you want to create the Perfect Shooter, give him 5 dots and specialist in the weapon of choice, it\u2019s boring. Now imagine you are a specialist in technology for anti-vehicle shots, or have a good training in medicine to pick the perfect spot to shoot, or a specialist in personal armor to go thru armored enemies. It gives a depth to the character even if you want to min max your char...</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand wanting &quot;not boring.&quot; But there needs to be a happy medium between not boring and not silly. I want my car to be not boring so my wheels are triangular instead of round. Is that boring? No. Is it silly? Very much.<br /> <br /> The Marine sniper sergeant doesn't put round after round into bullseye targets over the course of years or decades so he can be ready to... discuss the intricacies of 19th century British long-arm manufacturing at a university symposium. Likewise a tenured professor of history doesn't obtain a doctorate specializing in 19th century British long-arm manufacture so she can act as over-watch during a raid on a terrorist cell.<br /> <br /> The sergeant practices as he does to become really, really accurate with rifles. The professor studies as she does to be a world authority on her subject. Boring? Maybe. Silly? No.<br /> <br /> Now, there can be crossover. The sergeant's familiarity with rifles might let him hold an intelligent discussion with the professor. Meanwhile, if terrorists attacked the symposium leaving the defenders to fight back with antique weapons, the professor might be able to help, if nothing else than by helping the sergeant choose the best weapon. &quot;No, love. That's a Pattern 1859 Indian Service. You want the Pattern 1858, which is the one with the rifling. With the '59, you'd be more accurate spitting the bullets at them.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T21:08:10-08:00","id":1355334,"title":"","content":"You are reading it in the wrong direction. Your Sargent, to become the perfect shooter learned about science to understand how the wing, earths curve and the gravity affect the shot. His speciality is not Aim 5 (rifles), it can be, but it will help on maintaining the rifle and things like that, his speciality is Science 3 (Long range shooting).<br /> Another speciality can be Technology (armors) helping him to shoot armored targets. And another Culture (Military) to help identifying tatical military targets in the field.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think it\u2019s silly or boring.<br /> <br /> The point on Enhancements is different from successes in the dice. Enhancements get into counting to determine the effect of the success, not to determine if it was a success or not. Your enhancements are added only if you got at least one success in the test. So, to amin the bulls eye he needs more dice and not more enhancements, what he can get by dots and momentum, not by speciality.<br /> <br /> When you talk about getting extra advantage on shots (or any direct skill test) you need Edges and maybe skill tricks...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T02:34:15-08:00","id":1355352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355291#post1355291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand that. That's the part that makes this kind of silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, and had written a longer post going through why I do, but I've decided not to post it. Essentially it's not that people don't understand the mechanic, it's that they're unwilling to let go of assumptions forged from WoD/CoD and accept that this is a different system with different design principles.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, Storypath is designed to have a lot of dials and switches individual groups can use or not as they choose. If using Specialties as an Enhancement on the skill itself is what you want, go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T10:15:25-08:00","id":1355435,"title":"","content":"I love the System as is. It's flexible, I can already do with it what I want, it withstands (most of) my attempts to go hog-wild on it<br /> and the skill specialities are just plain fun BECAUSE they work differently. The Aim Skill Trick that let's you use your gun ON ANY<br /> skill for a short while is just an expansion off that. It dials it up to eleven, in exchange for a point of momentum, IIRC. I'd have to check.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it works brilliantly. And that the system is fun with plain humans says it all... although, I'd start at least with Talents.<br /> The bennies of picking powered perks and edges indeed are rather nice.<br /> <br /> The fun thing is that the specialties scale with the competence of the characters skill in question, which means that there is a nice decision<br /> to make for the player. Do they go for specialization or do they broaden their horizon skill wise? The difference between a Specialization of<br /> 1 or 3 points is remarkable and can turn things quite around or make them rather legendary. That decision can already be made during<br /> character creation, but most likely will far more often happen during actual play.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I love it overall. The skill system is the strongest part of the core offerings in my opinion, closely followed by the Talents.<br /> Add in the option of Templates, Societies and Paths... which gave me a headache at first, but I am more and more coming around of grokking, and all is well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9298-bhurano","name":"Bhurano","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T12:25:24-08:00","id":1355463,"title":"","content":"Again, if you already have Skill Tricks, and Edges, and Gifts that enhance the thing, why do you need Specialties to also enhance the thing in the same way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T13:00:58-08:00","id":1355471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355463#post1355463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, if you already have Skill Tricks, and Edges, and Gifts that enhance the thing, why do you need Specialties to also enhance the thing in the same way?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that\u2019s my position. There already is a mechanic for \u201cI have this skill rated high, and I get an additional bonus in a niche application of it\u201d - Skill Tricks.<br /> <br /> Specialties do something else, and are far more useful for doing something else than they would be as a lesser Skill Trick. I doubt we\u2019d be even having these conversations if they\u2019d called it something else, and people didn\u2019t bring their Storyteller mechanics baggage connected to the term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T17:54:23-08:00","id":1355536,"title":"","content":"Or, at least, the discussion would focus a lot more on how big the Specialty Enhancement gets.<br /> <br /> I think there's a fair debate on the value of Specialty Enhancement scaling like they do, because getting to a +3e is a fairly big boost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T22:23:16-08:00","id":1355588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355536#post1355536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, at least, the discussion would focus a lot more on how big the Specialty Enhancement gets.<br /> <br /> I think there's a fair debate on the value of Specialty Enhancement scaling like they do, because getting to a +3e is a fairly big boost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I think Bunyip is way underestimating just how much +3E is worth, but it's not a big deal and not worth trying to use Anydice to prove one way or another just to give some random Onyx Path hater some minor thing to blow up into &quot;Storypath is broken!&quot; And since everyone else seems to want to discuss what the bonus applies to more than they want to discuss how big the bonus is, I'd feel like I was just derailing it.<br /> <br /> For my part, I'm glad Specialties don't enhance the base skill. I just think anything above +1 enhancement is too drastic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T23:03:53-08:00","id":1355589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355588#post1355588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. I think Bunyip is way underestimating just how much +3E is worth</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think I am. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve made reference to it at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T23:08:32-08:00","id":1355590,"title":"","content":"I think part of the problem is that the value of +3e isn't a simple calculation. I think the +3e is oriented towards supplementing low rated Skills, where you have a small dice pool (and thus significant chance of failure) and aren't going to have a lot of other sources of Enhancements around. The complaints about it tend towards when two high level Skills (with Tricks, Edges, etc.) compliment each other.<br /> <br /> A character with Str 2, Close Combat 1, and Medicine 5 that has a Specialty that could apply to attacks isn't going to turn into a combat monster just because of a +3e. You're still failing a good number of rolls outright, and you're going to struggle against a decent Defense/Soft Armor when you do roll any successes. But it's also a good enough boost that with some teamwork/setup/etc. you could get a cool moment in where you inject someone with a drug, slice a tendon, or whatever.<br /> <br /> The problem is when it starts t get closer to Str 5, Close Combat 5, a few Close Combat Skill Tricks, some combat Edges, and then Medicine 5's +3e stacked on top of all that where it starts to put you over the top and finding a Specialty like that gives you a major boost over what should otherwise be equal foes. It becomes a must have to be competitive in upper level combat (or other conflicts).<br /> <br /> I think another possible house rule could be:<br /> <br /> The bonus from a Specialty can't increase your non-Scale based Enhancements above itself. So if you'd get +2e from a Specialty, and a +1e from equipment, you'd get +2e total instead of +3e. If you already have +4e from various sources, a +3e from a Specialty stops doing you any good.<br /> <br /> This would allow the +3e for shoring up lower dice-pool actions to play that role, without it becoming an optimization issue.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T01:30:14-08:00","id":1355601,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I kinda checked some of the math and I'm not so sure the enhancement thing is actually quite as big of a thing as I thought. If you have a really high dice pool, the enhancement is nearly guaranteed, right? But if you're playing tier 1-2, you actually need to get reasonably high up into the dice pool amount before the whiff chance stops eating into your enhancement bonus so much. Tier 3-4, a little less drastic but still there.<br /> <br /> That all being said, I've kinda decided that I like the idea of specialities giving extra dice instead of enhancement bonuses, due to a thing that Heavy Arms mentioned. Basically, dice are better if your starting pool is low and enhancement are better if your start pool is high. I like the idea of specialities helping more to shore up weaknesses in other fields than augmenting strengths.<br /> <br /> Worst case scenario though, if specialties are a bit overpowered, they're still a fairly minor thing and easily houseruled. It's probably a good sign that we're talking about minor issues like this in terms of the health of the ssytem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355589#post1355589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t think I am. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve made reference to it at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I misunderstood one of your posts,so sorry about that. My mechanical quibbles aren't that big of a deal, and I actually think I overestimated them a little (see above). Anyway, Storypath is a great system and you've been doing a good job of interacting with the player base presumably for no extra pay. So, like, basically, I'm saying it's appreciated and I don't want to get so far into the math analysis or semantics hole that I end up coming across as one of those people who ruins discussions for developers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T02:27:40-08:00","id":1355605,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s why the +5e must be a rule for all the games (as described for Aberrant). Piling up lots of enhancements increase the effect beyond the plausible.<br /> <br /> The +3e from Specialities added to a +3e quality weapon and a +2e situational b\u00f4nus put anyone on pair with a low level Nova or a experienced Psion. Locking it to +5 (I would say maxing piles of +1 on no more than +3, to pile up to +4 you need at least +2 from somewhere and for a +5 you need at least +3 from somewhere) makes scale more important and limit the effects of the Specialities high bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T04:15:40-08:00","id":1355610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355601#post1355601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That all being said, I've kinda decided that I like the idea of specialities giving extra dice instead of enhancement bonuses, due to a thing that Heavy Arms mentioned. Basically, dice are better if your starting pool is low and enhancement are better if your start pool is high. I like the idea of specialities helping more to shore up weaknesses in other fields than augmenting strengths.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the one problem this faces, is that it only really helps is you're still getting Enhancements from something.<br /> <br /> 3 dice + 3e has a high whiff factor, but you roll a success more often than not, and when you do you can perform a fairly high difficulty task successful. If it looks like a major roll, you can always toss Momentum behind it to reduce the whiff factor.<br /> <br /> 6 dice + 0e is very reliable at rolling at least one success, but is going to struggle to do anything but low difficulty tasks.<br /> <br /> So what you want out of &quot;shoring up weaknesses in other fields,&quot; is going to matter a lot here. Is shoring up being less reliable than an expert in that field, but capable of getting big rolls when the chips are down, or is it making sure you've got low difficulty rolls covered/<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T10:43:53-08:00","id":1355658,"title":"","content":"OK having started this thread after some discussion with my players, I wanted to double check my understanding of the mechanic as written, I wanted to get a feel for the intention of the mechanic. This is usually my approach before I begin pounding on (house ruling) a mechanic. The following is the text I intend on presenting to the players. I am throwing it out here for two reasons:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Any feedback regarding clarity, readability or flow.</li> <li>As a resource for any one else who wants to use it or is sparked by it for their own spin.</li> </ol><br /> Please note this is not a I'm right your wrong, it is just the use for my campaign. Keep in mind I really love the Storypath system, have tried to order every storypath books as released (funds permitting) and started a journey to convert Chronicles of Darkness an Exalted 3E (eyeing the new Essense project) to the Storypath system. Any house rule change I make is not a knock to the system but another compliment that I am using this system. It just needs slight tweaaking to fit my campaign or gaming style., which is true of almost every system I've ever touched over the years. Also I think when one or more players raise a question or concern with a mechanic (out of game) that as the Storyteller, Storyguide, GM you need to be able to answer or have dialog and be willing to make changes, if it helps.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Specialties</b><br /> <br /> A Specialty is narrowly focused expertise within a Skill. For example, Aim grants skill with all ranged weapons, but a character may have a Specialty in Pistols. If a Specialty applies to your situation add a 1-point Enhancement.The specialty could apply on the direct use of the skill or be applied to another situation that it could benefit, within reason. If you find yourself going to great lengths to justify a Specialty, it probably shouldn\u2019t apply.<br /> <br /> For example, a character might apply her Pistols Specialty from Aim to an action using her Culture Skill to suggest a deeper knowledge and understanding of gun shows than another character who is equally adept in Culture might have. The Storyguide is the ultimate arbiter of what constitutes a Specialty and what doesn\u2019t; Specialties that are too broad or too narrow can hurt the story or never come into play.<br /> <br /> Sometimes specific actions might require you to have a Specialty to simply perform that action. When something requires you to have a Specialty in a Skill to do the roll, it just unlocks the ability to take that action, it does not apply Enhancement to the roll. some examples could be ...<ul><li>Learning a new language unrelated to your origin, &quot;I come in pieces ...&quot;</li> <li>Performing medicine on a new species or xeno, &quot;Hmmm we don't have one of these ...&quot;</li> <li>A combat fighter space pilot using an FTL ship, &quot;Now I'm pointed away from the sun, I think ...&quot;</li> <li>Learning sorceries or mystic rites, &quot;Hmmm a void like black portal, cool, run ...&quot;</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>House Rule &amp; Reasoning Note</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Specialties were house ruled because you do not gain an enchancement with the primary skill that you spend time practising, perfecting and gaining <b>expertise</b> and you only gain the enhancement in the <b>other</b> skill. In a case of two equal skill levels, Aim 3 (to shoot with a pistol) compared to Command 3 (to intimidate with a pistol) your results gained an enhancement bonus of 100-300% for the <b>other</b> skill on a successful roll. This mechanic is counter-intuitive to the narrative description and use of the word &quot;<b>expertise</b>&quot; The final reason to house rule out the scaling plus 1 to 3 is to leave the unique and more powerful bonus to the realm of Skill Tricks.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 12-18-2019, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T11:18:59-08:00","id":1355662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355605#post1355605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s why the +5e must be a rule for all the games (as described for Aberrant). Piling up lots of enhancements increase the effect beyond the plausible.<br /> <br /> The +3e from Specialities added to a +3e quality weapon and a +2e situational b\u00f4nus put anyone on pair with a low level Nova or a experienced Psion. Locking it to +5 (I would say maxing piles of +1 on no more than +3, to pile up to +4 you need at least +2 from somewhere and for a +5 you need at least +3 from somewhere) makes scale more important and limit the effects of the Specialities high bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thats are really neat idea to consider, so your saying ...<br /> <br /> +1's (max at +3)<br /> +2's (max at +4)<br /> +3's (max at +5)<br /> <br /> Hmmmm","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T11:30:06-08:00","id":1355665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355590#post1355590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of the problem is that the value of +3e isn't a simple calculation. I think the +3e is oriented towards supplementing low rated Skills, where you have a small dice pool (and thus significant chance of failure) and aren't going to have a lot of other sources of Enhancements around. The complaints about it tend towards when two high level Skills (with Tricks, Edges, etc.) compliment each other.<br /> <br /> A character with Str 2, Close Combat 1, and Medicine 5 that has a Specialty that could apply to attacks isn't going to turn into a combat monster just because of a +3e. You're still failing a good number of rolls outright, and you're going to struggle against a decent Defense/Soft Armor when you do roll any successes. But it's also a good enough boost that with some teamwork/setup/etc. you could get a cool moment in where you inject someone with a drug, slice a tendon, or whatever.<br /> <br /> The problem is when it starts t get closer to Str 5, Close Combat 5, a few Close Combat Skill Tricks, some combat Edges, and then Medicine 5's +3e stacked on top of all that where it starts to put you over the top and finding a Specialty like that gives you a major boost over what should otherwise be equal foes. It becomes a must have to be competitive in upper level combat (or other conflicts).<br /> <br /> I think another possible house rule could be:<br /> <br /> The bonus from a Specialty can't increase your non-Scale based Enhancements above itself. So if you'd get +2e from a Specialty, and a +1e from equipment, you'd get +2e total instead of +3e. If you already have +4e from various sources, a +3e from a Specialty stops doing you any good.<br /> <br /> This would allow the +3e for shoring up lower dice-pool actions to play that role, without it becoming an optimization issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly how our discussion started.<br /> <br /> Several skills running parallel to each other seems to be when players would make heavy use/break the spirit of specialties.<br /> <br /> Skill Aim | Speacialty Pistols<br /> * Gain a better shot by considering the angles<br /> <br /> Skill Command<br /> * Used the pistol specialty to gain a an intimidation factor with a weapon<br /> <br /> Skill Humanities | Specialty Angles<br /> <br /> Again I'm not saying I would approve any use in this manner, it is all case by case, but I like to prevent to easy or low hanging fruit problem early on.<br /> <br /> And this discussion started first from my player misunderstanding of the mechanic.<br /> <br /> I had intially thought that it was some type of scale like 5 - other skill (max 3), so that it would benefit low level skills and not high level skills,<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 12-18-2019, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T11:38:30-08:00","id":1355668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355352#post1355352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree, and had written a longer post going through why I do, but I've decided not to post it. Essentially it's not that people don't understand the mechanic, it's that they're unwilling to let go of assumptions forged from WoD/CoD and accept that this is a different system with different design principles.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, Storypath is designed to have a lot of dials and switches individual groups can use or not as they choose. If using Specialties as an Enhancement on the skill itself is what you want, go for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355471#post1355471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that\u2019s my position. There already is a mechanic for \u201cI have this skill rated high, and I get an additional bonus in a niche application of it\u201d - Skill Tricks.<br /> <br /> Specialties do something else, and are far more useful for doing something else than they would be as a lesser Skill Trick. I doubt we\u2019d be even having these conversations if they\u2019d called it something else, and people didn\u2019t bring their Storyteller mechanics baggage connected to the term.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree I think there is some Storyteller baggage connected to the use of the Term Specialty, as I have run Chronicles, Exalted, VTR and some of my players have been in some of those games. I would also say the term has been used in a number of games and brings with it an understanding for right or wrong, so some TTRPG baggage as well. My biggest disparity comes from<br /> <br /> Name / Description / Mechanic<br /> Specialty / &quot;Expertise&quot; / Does not beneit the base skill (expertise?)<br /> <br /> In the end I made a house rule (as posted above) as specialties are not tied so deeply with the overall Storypath core rules that it will make or break anything.<br /> <br /> best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 12-18-2019, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T11:41:00-08:00","id":1355669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bhurano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355435#post1355435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the System as is. It's flexible, I can already do with it what I want, it withstands (most of) my attempts to go hog-wild on it<br /> and the skill specialities are just plain fun BECAUSE they work differently. The Aim Skill Trick that let's you use your gun ON ANY<br /> skill for a short while is just an expansion off that. It dials it up to eleven, in exchange for a point of momentum, IIRC. I'd have to check.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it works brilliantly. And that the system is fun with plain humans says it all... although, I'd start at least with Talents.<br /> The bennies of picking powered perks and edges indeed are rather nice.<br /> <br /> The fun thing is that the specialties scale with the competence of the characters skill in question, which means that there is a nice decision<br /> to make for the player. Do they go for specialization or do they broaden their horizon skill wise? The difference between a Specialization of<br /> 1 or 3 points is remarkable and can turn things quite around or make them rather legendary. That decision can already be made during<br /> character creation, but most likely will far more often happen during actual play.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I love it overall. The skill system is the strongest part of the core offerings in my opinion, closely followed by the Talents.<br /> Add in the option of Templates, Societies and Paths... which gave me a headache at first, but I am more and more coming around of grokking, and all is well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed, the Path, Path Skill and Skill Point build is the best version yet. <br /> What do you want to be? Great lets do it.<br /> So easy, so flexible!<br /> <br /> BAM! nailed it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T11:55:36-08:00","id":1355670,"title":"","content":"I wish they'd been called Skill Halos. Being good with one skill has a halo effect on another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T12:30:58-08:00","id":1355677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355670#post1355670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish they'd been called Skill Halos. Being good with one skill has a halo effect on another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or synergies as someone mentioned ealier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T19:05:45-08:00","id":1355742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355352#post1355352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree, and had written a longer post going through why I do, but I've decided not to post it. Essentially it's not that people don't understand the mechanic, it's that they're unwilling to let go of assumptions forged from WoD/CoD and accept that this is a different system with different design principles.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, Storypath is designed to have a lot of dials and switches individual groups can use or not as they choose. If using Specialties as an Enhancement on the skill itself is what you want, go for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to read your longer post. Maybe it's just the word, &quot;specialty&quot; that's throwing me. I take &quot;specialty&quot; as connoting &quot;especially good at&quot; in the context of a skill. &quot;Steve is a really talented chef, but his specialty is Korean-Mexican fusion cuisine.&quot; Set Steve to cook up some burgers and those will be good burgers. But let him at some bulgogi burritos and your tongue is in for an amazing treat.<br /> <br /> So, maybe instead of calling them specialties, call them trivias - aspects of a skill that can manifest as areas of expertise in other skills. If Billy Ray has a specialty in Rifles, he's better at using Rifles than he is with other missile weapons. If he has a Trivia in Rifle, he's as good with them as with any other missile weapon but also has a kind of all-encompassing understanding of Rifles that can apply to skills other than Aim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T21:57:05-08:00","id":1355764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355677#post1355677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or synergies as someone mentioned ealier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that was me, but apologies if I borrowed it from anyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T22:35:18-08:00","id":1355772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355764#post1355764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that was me, but apologies if I borrowed it from anyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that beats &quot;trivias&quot; for sure. I think there's a place for specialties <i>and</i> synergies. It is reasonable that someone who is &quot;specialized&quot; with some aspect of a skill is &quot;better&quot; with that skill under those circumstances. Maybe Specialties reduce base difficulties by 1 to a minimum of 1. If Billy Ray has a Rifle with Aim (Rifles) and he's shooting at a dude with Soft Armor that makes that a +2 Difficulty, his Specialty reduces that to +1 and only acts as an Enhancement if the Difficulty is already 1. Specialties only ever reduce the difficulty/enhance by 1. If Ray also has the Synergy, Rifles with Aim, he can potentially have a +3 Enhancement with skills other than Aim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T01:10:31-08:00","id":1355793,"title":"","content":"Skill Tricks already have that design space fairly well handled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T10:23:59-08:00","id":1355885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355793#post1355793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skill Tricks already have that design space fairly well handled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Skill Tricks come off more as minor Knacks more than anything else. The idea that Billy Ray can hack into a computer by bashing it with a rifle butt using the Gun Tool skill trick has nothing to do with his actual skill in using rifles. I think I've decided that Skill Tricks will be reserved for Talents (including Superiors) alone to use. They fit much better into the whole &quot;that really shouldn't have worked but it did&quot; thing that Talents have.<br /> <br /> I think I'll allow Specialties to be limited to up to three (one for each dot above two) but with the proviso that can spend Specialty &quot;slots&quot; to double or triple up on the difficulty reduction. So, if Billy Ray has 5 dots in Aim he could have Rifles3 as a Specialty. When Ray uses Rifles he reduces his Difficulty by 3 down to a minimum of 1, but that's the only Specialty he gets. Or he could have Rifles2, Pistols1 or Rifles1, Pistols1, Direct Fire Vehicles1 (Coilguns, lasers, etc instead of bombs or missiles). As usual, any Specialty that could reduce a Difficulty lower than 1 instead applies as an Enhancement. Even a world-class marksman still has a chance to miss or hit the wrong target (botch).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T10:43:48-08:00","id":1355892,"title":"","content":"The issue I have with giving enhancements to the skill with the specialty is it makes the 3rd, 4th, and 5th dots of a skill worth more than the 1st or 2nd, yet the cost stays the same, since you're getting 1 die + 1 enhancement for that skill, assuming you choose a specialty you think will come into play often. So it will skew character building towards a specific type of build.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T12:04:32-08:00","id":1355908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355892#post1355892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue I have with giving enhancements to the skill with the specialty is it makes the 3rd, 4th, and 5th dots of a skill worth more than the 1st or 2nd, yet the cost stays the same, since you're getting 1 die + 1 enhancement for that skill, assuming you choose a specialty you think will come into play often. So it will skew character building towards a specific type of build.</div> </div> </div> </div>You still have to buy the Specialties (after the first &quot;free&quot; one at char creation). So, dots 3/4/5 are worth more if you have Specialties because you're actively spending more. If Billy Ray wants to be &quot;super-specialized&quot; in Rifles and starts at Aim 2, that costs 39 XP, 30 for the base dots and 9 more for the specializations. The same thing is true for Synergies and Tricks. At char creation you get one of each &quot;free&quot; for skills that have three or more dots. So, if somebody finishes allocating their dots and ends with Aim, Close Combat and Medicine at 3 dots, they could be a Skill Synergy and Skill Trick into Medicine. Or a Trick in Aim and a Synergy in Medicine.<br /> <br /> So, say the person above has a Specialty with Rifles, the Skill Trick Gun Tool and a Synergy with Rifles at char. creeation. If he wants all that for Close Combat and Medicine, that's 18 XP.<br /> <br /> And I will say that I like this concept of Specialties, Synergies and Tricks. It's a neat reflections of the Gifts in terms of Luck (Tricks), Skill Aptitude (Specialties) and Attribute Aptitude (Synergies).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","user":"johntfs","date":". 12-19-2019, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T12:29:25-08:00","id":1355916,"title":"","content":"Except enhancements don't make you more likely to succeed. They only make you succeed better. By adding enhancements but not dice to other skills, you're not making yourself more likely to succeed with other skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T13:29:20-08:00","id":1355931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355916#post1355916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except enhancements don't make you more likely to succeed. They only make you succeed better. By adding enhancements but not dice to other skills, you're not making yourself more likely to succeed with other skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Practically speaking, you'll need more than one success to truly succeed with most difficult or complicated tasks. If you want to hit someone who has Defense 3 and inflict damage, you need four successes to succeed at that in non-game speak, even if the game considers one success to be succeedng.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T13:56:15-08:00","id":1355936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355931#post1355931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Practically speaking, you'll need more than one success to truly succeed with most difficult or complicated tasks. If you want to hit someone who has Defense 3 and inflict damage, you need four successes to succeed at that in non-game speak, even if the game considers one success to be succeedng.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You'll only need 3 successes unless they have soft armor; Inflict Damage is a 0-cost stunt. However, for non-combat applications, generally only 1 success is needed to succeed, even if there is a complication.<br /> <br /> Storypath is meant to encourage players allow players to make specialized or broadly-skilled characters which are both effective. It's a different mindset than previous Storytell* games. I know the players in the game I run have had trouble with it. They built characters with their skill dots focused into only a few skills, except for one. His character usually does almost as well as everyone else's because he has decent dice pools and can add enhancements from specialties. So, he may not be the best of the group, but he's almost always effective. If those specialized characters also got enhancements to their highest skills from those skills, he'd be well behind the pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T14:54:12-08:00","id":1355949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355885#post1355885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. Skill Tricks come off more as minor Knacks more than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>By... doing mechanical stuff that makes your performance with that Skill better in specific situation. You can also design your own Skill Tricks too.<br /> <br /> Having both [House Ruled Specialty] and Skill Tricks is redundant, especially with Edges already out there too. How may ways do we need to let you make a Skill you've invested in heavily better? What's the benefit of adding more?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea that Billy Ray can hack into a computer by bashing it with a rifle butt using the Gun Tool skill trick has nothing to do with his actual skill in using rifles. </div> </div> </div>I mean, it does, since it stems from his Aim Skill.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think I've decided that Skill Tricks will be reserved for Talents (including Superiors) alone to use. </div> </div> </div>OK, but this is a house rule for your games, not something that makes a point for considering the RAW. I personally think it's a bit harsh to Psions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355908#post1355908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Billy Ray wants to be &quot;super-specialized&quot; in Rifles and starts at Aim 2, that costs 39 XP, 30 for the base dots and 9 more for the specializations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... no?<br /> <br /> Increasing Aim 2 to Aim 5 gots 15 XP (5 XP for 3 dots).<br /> You only need to buy a Specialty once for 3 XP.<br /> <br /> So if you apply a RAW Specialty to it's own Skill, it only costs 18 XP (assuming it starts at 2, and not at 3 w/your free starting Specialty, which reduces the price to 10 XP).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The same thing is true for Synergies... </div> </div> </div>OK, while &quot;synergy&quot; might have been a better term to use, can we not act like it's now official to call RAW Specialties that? You're just going to muddy the conversation like this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T18:26:25-08:00","id":1355980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355936#post1355936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You'll only need 3 successes unless they have soft armor; Inflict Damage is a 0-cost stunt. However, for non-combat applications, generally only 1 success is needed to succeed, even if there is a complication.<br /> <br /> Storypath is meant to encourage players allow players to make specialized or broadly-skilled characters which are both effective. It's a different mindset than previous Storytell* games. I know the players in the game I run have had trouble with it. They built characters with their skill dots focused into only a few skills, except for one. His character usually does almost as well as everyone else's because he has decent dice pools and can add enhancements from specialties. So, he may not be the best of the group, but he's almost always effective. If those specialized characters also got enhancements to their highest skills from those skills, he'd be well behind the pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find for my game that the really important non-combat rolls are opposed or rolls vs NPC static value. I do not find the important rolls as 1 Difficulty rolls. Not says that's 100% of the time, just my mileage so far.<br /> <br /> Larceny/Stealth vs Perception<br /> Survival/Tracking vs Survival/Evading<br /> Pilot vs Pilot<br /> * Followed by a round of Integrity/Res or Com for &quot;Chicken&quot;<br /> Larceny/Fast Talking vs Empathy/Detect Lies<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":25095,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","user":"Graylion","date":". 12-19-2019, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T19:11:34-08:00","id":1355986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355949#post1355949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By... doing mechanical stuff that makes your performance with that Skill better in specific situation. You can also design your own Skill Tricks too.<br /> <br /> Having both [House Ruled Specialty] and Skill Tricks is redundant, especially with Edges already out there too. How may ways do we need to let you make a Skill you've invested in heavily better? What's the benefit of adding more?</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the harm? But that's a fair point. I'll define one of the Skill Tricks that can be taken as Skill Focus (Pick an aspect/subskill of a skill. The character gets -1 to difficulties when using that aspect). A character may take this Trick once per skill per dot over 5.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355949#post1355949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it does, since it stems from his Aim Skill.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How? He shoots the computer and that fixes it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355949#post1355949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, but this is a house rule for your games, not something that makes a point for considering the RAW. I personally think it's a bit harsh to Psions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking it over but I figure that Psions have Psi (and really good future equipment).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355949#post1355949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um... no?<br /> <br /> Increasing Aim 2 to Aim 5 gots 15 XP (5 XP for 3 dots).<br /> You only need to buy a Specialty once for 3 XP.<br /> <br /> So if you apply a RAW Specialty to it's own Skill, it only costs 18 XP (assuming it starts at 2, and not at 3 w/your free starting Specialty, which reduces the price to 10 XP).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I thought Skills were 10 XP per dot and they're just 5. Meanwhile, let's redefine &quot;specialties&quot; as Skill Trick: Skill Focus. In that case Billy Ray spends 15 XP to raise Aim from 2 to 5 and then buys Skill Focus Aim (Rifles1); Skill Focus Aim(Rifles2) and Skill Focus Aim (Rifles3) which costs 9 points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355949#post1355949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK, while &quot;synergy&quot; might have been a better term to use, can we not act like it's now official to call RAW Specialties that? You're just going to muddy the conversation like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine. I still say that &quot;Specialties&quot; is a silly thing to call something onlt tangentially related a skill.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T21:03:08-08:00","id":1355997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355986#post1355986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the harm?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Player frustration by having too many choices to pick from.<br /> <br /> 2) Difficulty in designing your own content because more options means more interactions to have to consider.<br /> <br /> 3) It's easier to created newbie traps and optimization points when you expand options.<br /> <br /> 4) Diluting what each is mean to represent as they're only so many mechanical widgets to apply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How? He shoots the computer and that fixes it? </div> </div> </div>Skill Tricks are meant to be things that strain &quot;realism.&quot; We know, in reality, that smacking electronics is not actually good for them. But TC is a game where it emulates genres were physics takes a backseat to tropes and narrative device.<br /> <br /> In reality, nobody would purposefully design an electronic lock that opens if the keypad is damaged. Locks need to stay locked, and any sort of tampering should trigger a lock down instead.<br /> <br /> In TC, you can shoot the panel to open the lock because that's the sort of action the game supports.<br /> <br /> In universe, the books provide the basis for handwaving these sorts of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm thinking it over but I figure that Psions have Psi (and really good future equipment). </div> </div> </div>Talents have Inspiration, and equipment is a wash since their foes have access to equal equipment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Meanwhile, let's redefine &quot;specialties&quot; as Skill Trick: Skill Focus. </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> You were replying to someone discussing the RAW vs. a different house rule idea, not your house rule.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fine. I still say that &quot;Specialties&quot; is a silly thing to call something onlt tangentially related a skill.<br /> </div> </div> </div>The criticism of the name has been acknowledged. But clear communication is more important for discussing the game. WtA's use of the word Gnosis is far, far, worse, but I'm not going to insist everyone talking about WtA to start calling it Essence instead.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T04:46:21-08:00","id":1356041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1355114-skill-specialties?p=1355997#post1355997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No.<br /> <br /> You were replying to someone discussing the RAW vs. a different house rule idea, not your house rule.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, now I have no real house rule. Specialties are specialties as the game defines them. To get my version of &quot;specialties&quot; I'm using the Skill Trick rules.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-26T19:39:23-08:00","id":1357151,"title":"","content":"A use for specialties I haven\u2019t seen mentioned before: mixed actions. If I\u2019m shooting a pistol while standing atop a moving car and my aim 5 (pistols) pool ends up higher than my pool to balance on the car, then I\u2019m not using the aim skill for the roll. I now get to apply that specialty to the shooting portion of the action\u2014as long as I can manage at least one success with the small dice pool. If my specialty enhancement is high enough then I can focus the dice on staying on the car, but still demonstrate my supreme pistol skills by hitting the target through the enhancements.<br /> <br /> (this can get shady if a PC goes 5 close combat and 5 aim, then tries to always get in close shooting and punching/kicking/grappling to benefit from one of the two specialties.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}